1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,215
Nicodemus was one of the most respected men in Israel.

2
00:00:03,215 --> 00:00:03,980
A Pharisee.

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:06,430
A ruler of the Jews.

4
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:11,070
He had status, education, and everything a religious man could want.

5
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:14,782
And yet, in John 3:2, he does something strange.

6
00:00:14,782 --> 00:00:17,033
He comes to Jesus by night.

7
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:18,255
Why at night?

8
00:00:18,255 --> 00:00:19,350
Because he was afraid.

9
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:24,550
A man like him could not be seen publicly with a wandering teacher from Galilee.

10
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:29,530
But he came anyway, because something in him knew Jesus was real.

11
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:36,112
He says, “Rabbi, we know that thou art a teacher come from God.” Jesus does not answer the compliment.

12
00:00:36,112 --> 00:00:38,630
He goes straight to the heart.

13
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:40,410
John 3:3.

14
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:44,329
“Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born again,

15
00:00:44,329 --> 00:00:47,670
he cannot see the kingdom of God.” Think about that.

16
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:53,715
Jesus is speaking to the most religious man in the room, and He tells him religion is not enough.

17
00:00:53,715 --> 00:00:55,750
Nicodemus did not need more knowledge.

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:57,790
He needed a new birth.

19
00:00:57,790 --> 00:00:59,359
Nicodemus is confused.

20
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:05,150
In verse 4 he asks, “How can a man be born when he is old?” He is thinking physically.

21
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:07,390
Jesus is speaking spiritually.

22
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:11,415
So in verse 8, Jesus explains: “The wind bloweth where it listeth,

23
00:01:11,415 --> 00:01:15,805
and thou hearest the sound thereof, but canst not tell whence it cometh,

24
00:01:15,805 --> 00:01:19,830
and whither it goeth: so is every one that is born of the Spirit.”

25
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:23,123
You cannot see the wind, but you can see what it does.

26
00:01:23,123 --> 00:01:25,370
The new birth works the same way.

27
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:28,810
You cannot control it, but you can see the change.

28
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:31,360
Then Jesus points to a story Nicodemus knew well.

29
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,925
John 3:14.

30
00:01:32,925 --> 00:01:35,929
“And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness,

31
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:41,325
even so must the Son of man be lifted up.” In the wilderness, people were dying from snake bites,

32
00:01:41,325 --> 00:01:44,830
and all they had to do was look at the bronze serpent and live.

33
00:01:44,830 --> 00:01:48,731
Jesus is saying that one day He would be lifted up on a cross,

34
00:01:48,731 --> 00:01:51,878
and everyone who looks to Him in faith would live.

35
00:01:51,878 --> 00:01:54,365
And then comes the verse the whole world knows.

36
00:01:54,365 --> 00:01:56,230
John 3:16.

37
00:01:56,230 --> 00:02:00,206
“For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son,

38
00:02:00,206 --> 00:02:03,312
that whosoever believeth in him should not perish,

39
00:02:03,312 --> 00:02:06,667
but have everlasting life.” Notice who heard it first.

40
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:08,130
Not a crowd.

41
00:02:08,130 --> 00:02:12,350
One man, in the dark, in secret, full of doubts.

42
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:16,070
God’s love was personal before it was global.

43
00:02:17,195 --> 00:02:18,860
Verse 17 makes it even clearer.

44
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:22,872
“For God sent not his Son into the world to condemn the world;

45
00:02:22,872 --> 00:02:28,438
but that the world through him might be saved.” Jesus did not come to crush Nicodemus.

46
00:02:28,438 --> 00:02:30,185
He came to save him.

47
00:02:30,185 --> 00:02:31,710
And did it work?

48
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:36,152
In John 19:39, after the crucifixion, Nicodemus appears again.

49
00:02:36,152 --> 00:02:41,850
This time in daylight, carrying about a hundred pounds of spices to bury Jesus.

50
00:02:41,850 --> 00:02:46,083
The man who once hid in the night now stands in the open.

51
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:47,910
That is what the new birth does.

